if grep -rqE -- 'Co-authored-b[y]' $PATHS reports/; then
    echo "a committed path carries a co-authorship trailer"
    exit 1
fi
echo "ok  no trailer"

say "staging"
git add -- $PATHS reports/
git -c core.fileMode=false status --short

git commit -q -F - <<'MSG'
Freeze the entry: the geometry rebuilt at its pins, every report regenerated, the seed average adopted

The freeze is a reproduction check, and it reproduced. The model that ships
is the one fixed at 208ccae. This commit records the decision the
pre-registered rule computed, rebuilds the OSM geometry from answers fetched
at each airport's own pin, regenerates every live report under the parameters
that ship, and checks that every figure comes back where the paper quotes it.

The decision. SEED_AVERAGE_ADOPTED is True. The rule of 19 September was fixed
before any figure existed and re-read under the parameters that ship, as the
pre-registration required, and reports/baseline.md's Seed averaging computes
Adopted: December gains 1.11 s against a floor of 0.23, July 1.46 against
0.54, and the average beats every single seed on both legs.

The rebuild, and the rule it needed. The first attempt, earlier on 26
September, took LSZH from a fallback mirror whose database ended on 6 May,
four months before its pin, and only the element comparison caught it. An
instance cannot serve a state it has not ingested, so an answer whose
osm3s.timestamp_osm_base precedes its pin is not the pinned answer, whatever
was requested. The client now refuses such an answer, sets that mirror aside
for the airport, gives the primary as many asks as the whole rotation had,
and stops rather than falls back when every mirror fails or refuses. The
sidecar data/raw/PINS.json records each answer's pin, instance, time and
database state, and pin_agreement fails a stamp before its pin. Refetched
under the rule, all eleven airports were answered by overpass-api.de from
databases of 2026-09-26T08:29:06Z to 08:44:16Z, every one after its pin; two
fallback answers were refused, both from a database of 2026-05-06T03:25:00Z.
Compared with the answers of 1 September, the eleven are identical in every
element and field, in order. Asked for LIRF at 2020-01-01, the same instance
returned 355 elements against 494, so it applies the pin. The 35 files under
data/processed/taxi_distance/ came back byte-identical.

A cached answer's bytes change on every fetch, because its header carries the
instance's stamp and the fetch time, so a report's footer now declares a
cached Overpass answer by the sha256 of its parsed elements, marked as such,
and check 8 reads a footer of either form with the function that writes it.
The five reports that read the cache verify that way, eleven answers each.

The regeneration. Every live report was regenerated in the order its declared
inputs dictate and verified against them after it ran. The ladder took
9 h 46 min and its 52 residual files came back byte-identical. Against the
parent no figure moved: each report moved in its generation date, its footer,
or prose these generators now compute or date, and nothing else.
check_paper.py --strict passes against the regenerated reports: 398 figures,
358 matched, 29 historical, 11 exempt, 0 unmatched.

The submission this tree builds, not uploaded:
data/submissions/funny-firefly_v5.parquet, sha256
8a10f3acd8d64ee332af78d8be8fbe3e030c9407d942ca42d940274e595cb16a, 215,876
rows, the mean of 5 seeds, built in 29 min 27 s; its manifest,
funny-firefly_v5.manifest.json, sha256
94d3d7a2e503c1f14406e893bf0f4c4b9efb2ca98e7d5f630049e91a4252a544, records
the parameters, the seeds and the route-length check, and was written from
195e15f with these changes uncommitted.

The pending list is empty, each item closed by the work: the paper's by
check_paper.py --strict against every regenerated report; the footers' by the
two reports the pinned rebuild regenerated with theirs, reports/taxi_routing.md
and reports/penalty_sensitivity.md, so REPORTS_WITHOUT_FOOTER is empty too;
and the pin's by eleven airports fetched at their pins, compared element by
element with the cache the matrices were built from, one control, and the
matrices compared after. check_provenance.py --strict, the freeze condition,
passes.

Also here: the stale generator prose the paper pass found, rewritten to say
what the reports say, and dated; the two prose figures that stood exempt as
pending, now computed from the geometry the run routes (Istanbul's axis
angle) or formatted from a registered constant (the null-rate tolerance); the
comments in taxiout.models and make_submission.py that still called the
saturation rung worth nothing or a measured negative; REBUILD_PINS and the
README's dated caveat about the fallback mirrors; and
scripts/commit_paper_pass.sh's fix to its worktree step.

BOOSTER_PARAMS and docs/paper.md are the parent's. Nothing is uploaded.
MSG

say "the commit"
git log -1 --stat --format='%h %s'

say "the commit's own tree, in a fresh worktree"
# A fresh worktree checks out tracked files only, so it has no challenge data,
# no OSM cache and no residuals, and keeps the three tracked files under data/;
# the paper's §2.3 cites one of them. There the provenance gate passes with
# every data input unverifiable, its --strict fails for that reason alone, and
# the paper's --strict passes.
wt="$work/worktree"
git worktree add -q --detach "$wt" HEAD
(
    cd "$wt"
    "$PY" -m pytest -q -rs > "$work/wt_pytest.txt" 2>&1 || {
        tail -30 "$work/wt_pytest.txt"
        exit 1
    }
    tail -3 "$work/wt_pytest.txt"
    "$PY" scripts/check_provenance.py > "$work/wt_provenance.txt" 2>&1 || {
        cat "$work/wt_provenance.txt"
        exit 1
    }
    grep -E "^provenance" "$work/wt_provenance.txt"
    "$PY" scripts/check_paper.py --strict > "$work/wt_paper.txt" 2>&1 || {
        tail -5 "$work/wt_paper.txt"
        echo "check_paper.py --strict fails in the committed tree"
        exit 1
    }
    echo "ok  check_paper.py --strict passes in the committed tree"
) || {
    git worktree remove --force "$wt"
    echo "the committed tree does not pass its own gates; no tag is made."
    exit 1
}
git worktree remove --force "$wt"

say "the tag"
git tag -a "$TAG" -F - <<'TAGMSG'
The freeze of the PRC Data Challenge 2026 entry of team funny-firefly.

The model is the five-seed average of the submission rung, under the
parameters fixed at 208ccae. The OSM geometry is rebuilt from answers fetched
at each airport's own pin, identical in every element to those of 1 September,
and the distance matrices are byte-identical. Every live report is regenerated
from this tree, check_provenance.py --strict and check_paper.py --strict both
pass, and nothing is pending.

The submission built from this tree, gitignored and not part of the tag:
funny-firefly_v5.parquet, sha256
8a10f3acd8d64ee332af78d8be8fbe3e030c9407d942ca42d940274e595cb16a.
TAGMSG
git show -s --format='%h %s' "$TAG^{commit}"
git for-each-ref --format='%(refname:short) %(objecttype) %(*objectname:short)' "refs/tags/$TAG"

say "done"
echo "Nothing is pushed. 'git show $TAG' to read it;"
echo "'git tag -d $TAG && git reset --hard HEAD^' to undo both."
